&lt;h1&gt;


  Building an Accessible Architecture Diagram Viewer with Archify, React, and Tailwind CSS
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At 2:47 AM, a screen reader user reported they couldn't close your architecture diagram modal—focus was trapped behind the overlay, and the only way out was refreshing the page. Worse, your performance monitoring showed 340ms of layout thrashing every time someone opened a large diagram. These aren't edge cases. They're production failures that stem from treating a diagram renderer as a simple &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; insert when it's actually a complete document with motion, export controls, and its own interaction model.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I evaluated &lt;code&gt;tt-a1i/archify&lt;/code&gt; as an external integrator to solve one specific problem: displaying a motion-enabled, self-contained architecture diagram inside a React application without breaking screen reader navigation or forcing repeated layout recalculation. Archify's useful boundary is its generated HTML artifact. The diagram owns rendering, animation, and export. The host application owns routing, permissions, loading state, and the accessible shell around the artifact. Keeping those responsibilities separate prevents a diagram renderer from becoming a second application framework inside your product.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The production failure mode
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A common implementation animates diagram container &lt;code&gt;width&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;height&lt;/code&gt; from JavaScript. Every frame, the browser recalculates layout, repaints the viewport, and composites layers. On diagrams with 40+ nodes, this creates visible jank—especially when users resize the preview or change zoom levels.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The second failure is silent but more destructive: a hand-rolled modal often leaves focus behind the overlay. A screen reader user continues navigating the page while the diagram appears open. Pressing Escape may close the visual layer without returning focus to the trigger. The user is now lost in the DOM with no audible indication of where they are.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following component uses Radix Dialog for focus trapping, Escape handling, focus restoration, and ARIA semantics. Archify's generated HTML is passed as &lt;code&gt;srcDoc&lt;/code&gt;, appropriate when the artifact comes from a trusted build step. The iframe receives a meaningful accessible name and a restrictive sandbox. If the diagram needs scripts, &lt;code&gt;allow-scripts&lt;/code&gt; is sufficient—avoid adding &lt;code&gt;allow-same-origin&lt;/code&gt; unless the artifact genuinely requires it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@radix-ui/react-dialog"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;X&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"lucide-react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ArchitecturePreviewProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ArchitecturePreview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Interactive architecture diagram preview"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ArchitecturePreviewProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Trigger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asChild&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"rounded-md bg-slate-900 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white
                     shadow-sm transition hover:bg-slate-700 focus:outline-none
                     focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500
                     focus-visible:ring-offset-2"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Open&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;diagram&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Trigger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Portal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Overlay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fixed inset-0 z-40 bg-slate-950/70 data-[state=open]:animate-fade-in"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Content&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;aria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;describedby&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"architecture-preview-description"&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fixed inset-4 z-50 flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl
                     border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-2xl outline-none
                     sm:inset-8 lg:inset-12"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 border-b border-slate-200 p-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"text-base font-semibold text-slate-950"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Description&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"architecture-preview-description"&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600"&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Close&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asChild&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;aria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Close diagram preview"&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"rounded-md p-2 text-slate-500 hover:bg-slate-100
                           hover:text-slate-900 focus:outline-none
                           focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500"&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;X&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;aria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hidden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"true"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;18&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Close&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"diagram-frame min-h-0 flex-1 bg-slate-50 p-3"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iframe&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${title} architecture diagram`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="n"&gt;srcDoc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="n"&gt;sandbox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"allow-scripts"&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="n"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"lazy"&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"h-full w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white"&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Portal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The critical detail isn't the modal styling—it's the ownership model. Radix manages interaction state and focus. The iframe isolates Archify's document and prevents diagram styles from leaking into the host application. Tailwind handles the stable shell without requiring JavaScript measurements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Configuration as an explicit build boundary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generate the diagram before deployment or in a controlled server-side job, then supply it to the React component as an artifact. A small configuration file makes this boundary reproducible:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight yaml"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# archify.config.yaml
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;./architecture/system.md&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;output&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;./public/diagrams/system.html&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;slate&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;motion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;enabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;durationMs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;420&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;prefersReducedMotion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;formats&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1920&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1080&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;security&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;sandbox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;allow-scripts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The exact command depends on the repository's CLI surface, but the architectural intent remains stable: source content transforms into a self-contained HTML deliverable, and the React application consumes that deliverable rather than reconstructing the diagram at runtime.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  CSS micro-interaction without layout thrashing
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use transforms and opacity for interaction feedback. Reserve container queries for responsive behavior inside the component rather than reading element dimensions in JavaScript.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@keyframes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;fade-in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;opacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;translateY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.35rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;scale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.99&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;opacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;translateY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;scale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@keyframes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;diagram-pulse&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;box-shadow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;rgb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;59&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;130&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;246&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;box-shadow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.35rem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;rgb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;59&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;130&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;246&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@container&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;min-width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;48rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;.diagram-frame&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;padding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.25rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;.diagram-frame&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iframe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;animation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;diagram-pulse&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;2.8s&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ease-in-out&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@media&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;prefers-reduced-motion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;.diagram-frame&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iframe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data-state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"open"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.data-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;\=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;animate-fade-in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;animation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;none&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In a Tailwind v4 project, register the animation utility in the application stylesheet if it isn't already available:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nv"&gt;--animate-fade-in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fade-in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;180ms&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ease-out&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;both&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This avoids the tempting but expensive pattern of updating inline width and height on every pointer event. The browser can usually composite transforms without recalculating the entire document layout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Practical trade-offs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An iframe adds a document boundary and makes cross-document communication less convenient. That's a worthwhile cost when Archify exports a complete HTML experience with its own motion and controls. A direct React renderer would provide tighter state integration, but it would also couple the application to diagram internals and increase the chance of CSS, focus, and lifecycle conflicts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A trusted &lt;code&gt;srcDoc&lt;/code&gt; artifact is also a security boundary only when its generation pipeline is controlled. Don't interpolate user-authored HTML without sanitization. If diagrams are user-generated, sanitize before storage and consider serving them from a separate origin with a restrictive Content Security Policy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The resulting architecture is deliberately modest: Archify produces the visual artifact, the iframe isolates it, Radix owns modal accessibility, and Tailwind styles the host shell. That separation addresses the real failure modes—layout thrashing and broken focus navigation—without turning a diagram preview into an unmaintainable custom UI subsystem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hardest operational dilemma here is deciding when the iframe boundary becomes more costly than direct integration. If your diagrams need bidirectional state sync with the host application—live editing, real-time collaboration, or deep keyboard navigation across diagram nodes—the document boundary starts working against you. At that point, you're building a tightly coupled diagram editor, not a viewer, and the architecture needs to change accordingly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How are you handling architecture diagram rendering in production applications? Have you hit the layout thrashing ceiling, or are you dealing with something worse—focus traps, memory leaks from unmounted SVG, or accessibility complaints you can't reproduce? I'd like to hear what broke and how you fixed it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most React tutorials stop at the same place: &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;, props, maybe context. Then they stop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The real questions come after that. Why does my component re-render? What happens during the commit phase? How does hydration work? What is a custom renderer?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I found a curriculum that answers those. It's on &lt;strong&gt;KandZ Tuts&lt;/strong&gt;, and it's 131 chapters, organized as a single progression from your first component to React's internal architecture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's the breakdown.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Foundations (1–14)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What React is, Node.js and package managers, creating a project with Vite, project structure, JSX syntax and rules, embedding JavaScript expressions, functional components, importing and exporting, props, default props, the &lt;code&gt;children&lt;/code&gt; prop, event listeners, passing handlers as props, and the synthetic event object.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  State (15–24)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;, updating primitive state, updating state from previous state, updating objects and arrays in state, conditional rendering with &lt;code&gt;if&lt;/code&gt;/ternary/logical AND, rendering lists with &lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;, and the importance of keys.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Forms (25–29)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Controlled inputs, textareas and selects, handling multiple inputs with one handler, form submission and &lt;code&gt;preventDefault&lt;/code&gt;, and uncontrolled inputs with &lt;code&gt;useRef&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Effects and Data (30–34)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;, dependency array rules, cleanup functions, fetching API data, and handling loading and error states.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Custom Hooks and Context (35–41)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Extracting reusable logic, the prop drilling problem, &lt;code&gt;createContext&lt;/code&gt;, providing and consuming context, &lt;code&gt;useReducer&lt;/code&gt;, and combining context with &lt;code&gt;useReducer&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Refs, Memoization, and Modern Hooks (42–57)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useRef&lt;/code&gt; for DOM access and mutable values, &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useImperativeHandle&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useLayoutEffect&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useDebugValue&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useTransition&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useSyncExternalStore&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useOptimistic&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useActionState&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useFormStatus&lt;/code&gt;, and the &lt;code&gt;use&lt;/code&gt; hook.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Routing and State Libraries (58–70)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Router (route elements, outlets, dynamic params, programmatic navigation, protected and nested routes), TanStack Query (setup, &lt;code&gt;useQuery&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useMutation&lt;/code&gt;, cache invalidation), Redux Toolkit (provider, slices, actions, reducers, middleware, thunks), and Zustand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Styling and Forms (71–75)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CSS Modules, Tailwind CSS, styled-components and Emotion, React Hook Form, and Zod integration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Advanced Patterns (76–87)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Code splitting with &lt;code&gt;React.lazy&lt;/code&gt;, Suspense, error boundaries, render props, higher-order components, compound components, control props, portals, React Testing Library, user interaction testing, MSW, and Playwright.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  SSR and Frameworks (88–95)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SSR vs SSG, React Server Components architecture, Server Components vs Client Components rules, Server Actions, Next.js App Router, layouts and loading UI, streaming SSR and progressive hydration, and micro-frontends with Module Federation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Production and Accessibility (96–100)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation and focus management, XSS prevention, React DevTools profiling, and production builds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  React Internals (101–109)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fiber architecture and reconciliation, the commit phase vs render phase, double-pass rendering and Strict Mode, the concurrent rendering scheduler and priorities, automatic batching, memory leak prevention, synthetic event pooling and delegation, hydration mismatch errors, and progressive and selective hydration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Advanced Frameworks (110–114)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SSG with React frameworks, Incremental Static Regeneration, Partial Prerender, React Server Functions and the wire format, and the Taint APIs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Applied React (115–120)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;i18n and localization, XState state machines, WebSockets, offline-first apps with service workers, monorepos with Turborepo and Nx, and building reusable component libraries with Storybook.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Beyond the Browser (121–130)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Native core, React Native navigation and native modules, Electron and Tauri, React Three Fiber, WebGL and Canvas, React Konva, the Web Audio API, Web Components integration, custom Babel/SWC plugins, and custom React renderers with &lt;code&gt;react-reconciler&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Chapter 131: The Complete Cheatsheet
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Why the Internals Section Matters
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Chapters 101–109 are the reason to read this curriculum.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most resources stop at "here's how &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; works." This one goes into &lt;strong&gt;how React actually renders&lt;/strong&gt;—Fiber, reconciliation, the commit phase, the concurrent scheduler, automatic batching, hydration mismatches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's what lets you diagnose a performance problem instead of guessing at &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;. It's the difference between using React and understanding it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The &lt;code&gt;use&lt;/code&gt; Hook and React 19
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Chapters 54–57 cover the hooks that define modern React: &lt;code&gt;useOptimistic&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useActionState&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useFormStatus&lt;/code&gt;, and the &lt;code&gt;use&lt;/code&gt; hook.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are not footnotes. They are how React 19 handles async forms, optimistic updates, and reading promises in render. A curriculum that skips them is teaching React from two years ago.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Beyond the Browser
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Chapters 121–130 are unusual. Most React curricula stop at the web. This one covers React Native, Electron, Tauri, React Three Fiber, React Konva, the Web Audio API, and custom renderers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you've wondered how React renders to a canvas, a native mobile view, or a 3D scene, this is where that gets explained.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Who This Is For
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Beginners:&lt;/strong&gt; Start at Chapter 1 and read in order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Experienced React developers:&lt;/strong&gt; Jump to Chapter 57 (the &lt;code&gt;use&lt;/code&gt; hook), Chapter 101 (Fiber), or Chapter 108 (hydration mismatches) if those are gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Developers moving beyond the web:&lt;/strong&gt; Start at Chapter 121.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The Link
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://tuts.kandz.me/category/programming/frontend-fed/react-ecosystem/react/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React — KandZ Tuts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Free, no signup, 131 chapters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you've been writing React for years but never understood what the scheduler does, or you're starting from scratch and want a path that doesn't stop at &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;, this is the most complete free curriculum I've found.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;What React topics do you wish had better free resources? Let me know in the comments.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most AI support agents answer in paragraphs. Your user asks "how do I export my contacts?" and gets three sentences telling them to open Settings, then Data, then Export. Then they go hunting for each button.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I build &lt;a href="https://clickalong.ai/?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=listing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Clickalong&lt;/a&gt;, an AI support agent that answers from your docs and then points at each button in your app until the task is done. This post shows how to add it to a SaaS app, from a plain HTML page up to a React app with signed-in users.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Create a workspace and load your docs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sign up at clickalong.ai and paste your help center link. Clickalong imports the articles, and the agent answers only from them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No help center yet? Write articles in the dashboard, or let your coding agent draft them with our open-source skill:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx skills add clickalong/clickalong-agent-skills --skill write-clickalong-docs
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Add the widget
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On a plain HTML site, one tag goes before &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;/body&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"https://clickalong.ai/widget.js"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;data-key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"pk_your_key"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;data-clickalong&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Your key is on the Install page in the dashboard.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. In a React app, use the SDK
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bundled apps get a typed loader, &lt;code&gt;@clickalong/sdk&lt;/code&gt;. It has no dependencies, does nothing during server rendering, and is safe under React Strict Mode.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install @clickalong/sdk
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"use client"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Clickalong&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@clickalong/sdk"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ClickalongWidget&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Clickalong&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"pk_your_key"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Clickalong&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;identify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Render it once in your root layout: &lt;code&gt;app/layout.tsx&lt;/code&gt; in Next.js, &lt;code&gt;app/root.tsx&lt;/code&gt; in React Router. Conversations now follow the user across devices, and your team sees who they're talking to.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Want the Verified badge? Pass a &lt;code&gt;userHash&lt;/code&gt; as well. It's an HMAC-SHA256 of the lowercased email, computed on your server with the identity secret from Settings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. Pass app state
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Clickalong&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"pro"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;seats&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;These values show next to the conversation, so whoever picks up a handed-over chat sees the user's plan without asking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Teach it the clicks
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the part that makes it more than a chatbot. Install the &lt;a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/clickalong-recorder/mlmmampfbhgplpnblnhfpidmficcifcb" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Clickalong Recorder&lt;/a&gt; Chrome extension, click through a task once (say, changing a plan), and save it as a tour. Next time a user asks how to change their plan, the agent answers and then walks them through it, one highlighted button at a time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No recorded tour for a task? The agent can still guide from your help articles with "Show me".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What you get
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI support agent that answers from your docs, in the user's language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guided tours that point at the real buttons in your app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A shared inbox for chats the AI hands over&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One flat price per workspace with unlimited conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The widget and inbox are free. The AI agent starts on the Mini plan, and guided tours and "Show me" start on Essentials. &lt;a href="https://clickalong.ai/pricing?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=listing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;See pricing&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href="https://clickalong.ai/?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=listing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;start free&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the past few weeks I've been building &lt;a href="https://hyroxpacer.site" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HYROX Pacer&lt;/a&gt; — a free, no-login web app that helps HYROX athletes plan their race: target finish time, 8×1km running splits, 8 station target times, and Roxzone transitions, all in one place.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Why
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;HYROX is booming, but race planning is scattered across spreadsheets, forum posts and YouTube videos. I wanted one interactive tool where you pick your division (Open / Pro / Doubles), set a target time or pace, and get station-by-station splits you can actually race with.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  What it does
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Target time &amp;amp; splits&lt;/strong&gt; — enter a goal finish time or pace and get per-lap and per-station targets&lt;/li&gt;
