&lt;p&gt;Your page looks right on your laptop and scrolls sideways on your phone: this guide finds what is too wide and fixes the usual causes one at a time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The examples here are screenshots; they run live in &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/a-layout-that-works-on-every-screen/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;the original article&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You will build a small travel page that breaks on a phone the way real pages do, look at it the way a phone does, find the parts that stick out, and fix each one. At the end the same page is one column on a phone and two columns on a laptop. You need a React app with Box Kite installed; if you do not have one yet, steps 1 and 2 of &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/start-building-with-box-kite/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Your first web page with Box Kite&lt;/a&gt; take two minutes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 1: build a page that breaks
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Replace everything in &lt;code&gt;src/App.tsx&lt;/code&gt; with this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@box-kite/react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Flex&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@box-kite/react/components/flex'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
