&lt;p&gt;At phone width the last links now start a second line, and none of them is cut off at the edge. The page still scrolls, because of the other two culprits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 5: one column on a phone, two on a laptop
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two columns side by side do not fit in 390 pixels. Write the phone layout first and add the laptop layout on top of it: &lt;code&gt;d="column"&lt;/code&gt; stacks the sidebar above the story, and &lt;code&gt;md={{ d: 'row' }}&lt;/code&gt; puts them side by side from 768 pixels up. Every prop works this way: the plain prop is for every screen, and &lt;code&gt;sm&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;md&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;lg&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;xl&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;xxl&lt;/code&gt; override it from 640, 768, 1024, 1280 and 1536 pixels.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sidebar's fixed width goes the same way: no width on a phone, so it takes the whole column, and a quarter of the page from &lt;code&gt;md&lt;/code&gt; up. &lt;code&gt;'1/4'&lt;/code&gt; is a fraction of the parent's width, and &lt;code&gt;flexShrink: 0&lt;/code&gt; keeps the sidebar at that quarter instead of letting a wide photo squeeze it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

